# 40: walk the cursor onto the APPENDED wheel cell 0x11 (Pyron's native
# vs2 id) and pick it. Path from the default Demitri cell 0x01, derived
# from vsavj's own TABLE B plus the wheel extension's inbound edges
# (build/manifest/wheel_layout_proposed.json):
#   D -> 0x06 , D -> 0x08 , DR -> 0x0B , D -> 0x11 (edges_in: 0x0B D -> 0x11)
# Note the third press is DR, not D: vanilla 0x08 D reaches 0x0B, but the
# extension REWIRES 0x08 D to Huitzil's cell 0x10, so the diagonal is the
# route to the random cell that carries Pyron's inbound edge.
# BUILD-ONLY replay: on vanilla vsavj the final D lands back on 0x0B —
# this script is meaningful only on a build carrying the extended wheel
# AND a tenant at id 0x11. The 0x10 twin is replay 37, the 0x13 twin 36.
300-305 sys=C1
800-803 sys=S1
1000-1002 p1=D
1040-1042 p1=D
1080-1082 p1=DR
1120-1122 p1=D
1700-1702 p1=1
3600 wait
